<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42750" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sătyrĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σατυρικός.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to Satyrs</i>,
				<i>like Satyrs</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">signa,</span>”
				i. e. <i>misshapen figures resembling Satyrs</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 4</span></i>
			. 19, § 50.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to</i> (Greek)
				<i>satire</i>, <i>satiric</i> (cf.
			satiricus, with which the word is often confounded): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus scenarum (with tragicum and comicum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					5, 6, 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>heating</i>, <i>exciting</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">medicamenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Acut. 2, 18</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
